                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "804801d2-ae74-425a-8c8d-cf139e1fd2cb",
                                "sense_id": "528a7591-0c29-3068-818a-0f09e35fa7e3",
                                "text": "Critically more trustworthy, and exegetically very valuable, is Bernhard Weiss, Das Leben Jesu (3d ed. 1889, 2 vols.), translated from the first ed., The Life of Christ (1883, 3 vols.)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1db6c107-2d08-4dbc-9ad4-456382e3d9c0",
                                "sense_id": "528a7591-0c29-3068-818a-0f09e35fa7e3",
                                "text": "And, if exegetically handled, it must mean that Walker, junr., is to continue spinning and spelling, as also once a week reading the Town and Country Magazine, all the days of his life."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "02f8cae8-c412-4a0a-b3b6-9ce5a418b780",
                                "sense_id": "528a7591-0c29-3068-818a-0f09e35fa7e3",
                                "text": "It was a favorite passage this, and he often threatened to treat it exegetically; laughing heartily when I said, in that case, he would not have great trouble with the context, which in others cost him a good deal."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
